{537}{No more questions.  Now what were you saying?}{}{5}{lc1 5}{175}{}
{538}{None for now.  I'm ready to continue our alliance...}{}{5}{lc1 6}{324}{}
{541}{I was the first of the Necromancers, and the Elven council was displeased with my studies into the darker side of that discipline.  After an inquiry into my activities, the council was going to exile me, but Arronax, in his hatred of me, convinced them banishment was more appropriate for my so-called "crimes".  They banished me soon after...}{I was the first of the Necromancers, and the Elven council was displeased with my studies into the darker side of that discipline.  After an inquiry into my activities, the council was going to exile me, but Arronax, in his hatred of me, convinced them banishment was more appropriate for my so-called "crimes".  They banished me soon after...}{}{78}{}{}
{542}{I see.  A few more questions...}{}{5}{}{528}{}
{544}{Arronax was banished here only a few years after I was.  After seeing how powerful I'd become, he raised a ragged army against me, but his efforts were useless.  I destroyed his army, and threw him in chains.  A fitting end for him, and a reward for his endless arrogance...}{Arronax was banished here only a few years after I was.  After seeing how powerful I'd become, he raised a ragged army against me, but his efforts were useless.  I destroyed his army, and threw him in chains.  A fitting end for him, and a reward for his endless arrogance...}{}{79}{}{}
{545}{I see.  A few more questions...}{}{5}{}{528}{}
{547}{The Dark Elves began calling across the Void soon after Arronax had been banished.  By the time their feeble cries were heard, their master was already defeated and imprisoned.  Pretending I was he, I masterminded the manipulation of the Panarii, coerced the Dark Elves into betraying the trust of Loghaire and the Wheel Clan, and had the Black Mountain Clan sent to me.}{The Dark Elves began calling across the Void soon after Arronax had been banished.  By the time their feeble cries were heard, their master was already defeated and imprisoned.  Pretending I was he, I masterminded the manipulation of the Panarii, coerced the Dark Elves into betraying the trust of Loghaire and the Wheel Clan, and had the Black Mountain Clan sent to me.}{}{80}{}{}
{548}{And what has the Black Mountain Clan been doing?}{}{5}{}{551}{}
{549}{Interesting.  A few more questions...}{}{5}{}{528}{}
{551}{The Black Mountain Clan was brought here because of the nature of technology and magick...the wards which bind the gate back to Arcanum are weakening because of the rise of technology.  I've brought the dwarves here to construct a device to shatter the wards once and for all...}{The Black Mountain Clan was brought here because of the nature of technology and magick...the wards which bind the gate back to Arcanum are weakening because of the rise of technology.  I've brought the dwarves here to construct a device to shatter the wards once and for all...}{}{81}{}{}
{552}{I see.  A few more questions...}{}{5}{}{528}{}
{554}{I want the end to all life.  I've divined the mysteries of death, and seen its truth.  Death is the natural state of things, and life is a distortion of the natural order.  I will put an end to it, once and for all...}{I want the end to all life.  I've divined the mysteries of death, and seen its truth.  Death is the natural state of things, and life is a distortion of the natural order.  I will put an end to it, once and for all...}{}{82}{}{}
{555}{I see.  A few more questions...}{}{5}{}{528}{}
{557}{Splendid.  I've spent the last 2000 years developing my philosophy, but I'm always eager to hear another's thoughts.  Please, proceed...}{Splendid.  I've spent the last 2000 years developing my philosophy, but I'm always eager to hear another's thoughts.  Please, proceed...}{}{83}{}{}
{558}{Very well.  Let's speak of the nature of life and death...}{}{5}{}{564}{re 5}
{564}{Yes...let us speak of this.  It is my opinion that the nature of life is accidental, that this reality we experience is merely a distortion of death.  What say you, traveler?}{Yes...let us speak of this.  It is my opinion that the nature of life is accidental, that this reality we experience is merely a distortion of death.  What say you, traveler?}{}{84}{}{}
{565}{As you've said, I have only my experience to draw from...}{}{5}{gf2668 1}{570}{lc1 0}
{566}{I think you're making generalizations...open your eyes...}{}{5}{gf2668 1}{640}{}
{567}{As you've said, I have only my experience to draw from...}{}{5}{gf2669 1}{570}{}
{568}{I think you're making generalizations...open your eyes...}{}{5}{gf2669 1}{640}{}
{570}{Yes...but what has that experience taught you?  I know not the roads you've traveled, but I do know that all living things feel pain and loss...its my opinion that they feel these things because they were NEVER meant for what we know as life...their souls are not equipped for it...}{Yes...but what has that experience taught you?  I know not the roads you've traveled, but I do know that all living things feel pain and loss...its my opinion that they feel these things because they were NEVER meant for what we know as life...their souls are not equipped for it...}{}{85}{}{}
{571}{Experience has taught me that fanaticism is dangerous...}{}{5}{}{646}{}
{572}{Hold, Kerghan. That assumption is based on YOUR experience...}{}{5}{gf2668 1}{576}{                  }
{573}{Isn't it presumptuous of you to make that decision for everyone?}{}{5}{}{646}{}
{576}{[Kerghan is silent for a moment, considering.]  Yes, you're correct.  I concede you that point.  But!  I have seen both sides, where as you have only the lands of the living.  Trust me when I say that the souls who are called back to this life are in the most excruciating pain...its unnatural...}{[Kerghan is silent for a moment, considering.]  Yes, you're correct.  I concede you that point.  But!  I have seen both sides, where as you have only the lands of the living.  Trust me when I say that the souls who are called back to this life are in the most excruciating pain...its unnatural...}{}{86}{}{}
{577}{Maybe your opinions bias your observations?}{}{5}{}{652}{}
{578}{I think you're refusing to see the truth...}{}{5}{}{652}{}
{579}{Yes, but perhaps that is the nature of those particular souls...}{}{5}{}{582}{}
{582}{What do you mean?  Are you faulting the souls of the dead for the meddling of the living?}{What do you mean?  Are you faulting the souls of the dead for the meddling of the living?}{}{87}{}{}
{583}{No.  Some souls are in pain because they hold on too tightly...}{}{5}{}{588}{}
{584}{No, but it's fate that some will suffer and some rest in peace...}{}{5}{}{658}{}
{585}{There's no rhyme nor reason.  It's just the way things are...}{}{5}{}{658}{}
{588}{But you speak as if these souls have a choice when they're brought back!  It's the mindless bravado of the living that subjects them to the vagaries of this life...!}{But you speak as if these souls have a choice when they're brought back!  It's the mindless bravado of the living that subjects them to the vagaries of this life...!}{}{88}{}{}
{589}{Even the dead have a choice...the blame is theirs...}{}{5}{}{663}{}
{590}{No, but the PAIN is of their own making...}{}{5}{}{594}{}
{591}{Of course. They shouldn't come back if they don't want to...}{}{5}{}{663}{}
{594}{[Kerghan seems ready to respond, but then falls silent.]  I'm willing to say you might be correct.  But what proof have you?}{[Kerghan seems ready to respond, but then falls silent.]  I'm willing to say you might be correct.  But what proof have you?}{}{89}{}{}
{595}{What proof do I need?  Your state is the only proof necessary...}{}{5}{}{669}{}
{596}{Think about it. The pain is from LOSS of life, not because of it...}{}{5}{gf2070 0}{603}{}
{597}{I've spoken with souls who weren't in pain...}{}{5}{gf2070 1}{600}{}
{600}{Just because some souls have accepted the nature of this distortion doesn't justify its existence.  If what you're saying is correct, then what is the nature of death, of life?  Which is the natural state?  Why is there pain on one side, and uncertainty on the other?}{Just because some souls have accepted the nature of this distortion doesn't justify its existence.  If what you're saying is correct, then what is the nature of death, of life?  Which is the natural state?  Why is there pain on one side, and uncertainty on the other?}{}{90}{}{}
