{603}{There may be truth in your words.  Assuming you're right, then what causes this distortion? What is the nature of death, of life?  Which is the natural state?  Why is there pain on one side, and uncertainty on the other?}{There may be truth in your words.  Assuming you're right, then what causes this distortion? What is the nature of death, of life?  Which is the natural state?  Why is there pain on one side, and uncertainty on the other?}{}{91}{}{}
{604}{The distortion is caused by the eyes with which we choose to see...}{}{5}{}{606}{}
{606}{[Kerghan looks away, visibly troubled.]  Perhaps it is my own arrogance, my own bravado, that has brought us here, to this crossroads.  The question is...where to go from here?  We've spoken of fate, of prophecy.  Have I traveled this road too long to turn back?  Perhaps I have no choice but to continue on to the end...}{[Kerghan looks away, visibly troubled.]  Perhaps it is my own arrogance, my own bravado, that has brought us here, to this crossroads.  The question is...where to go from here?  We've spoken of fate, of prophecy.  Have I traveled this road too long to turn back?  Perhaps I have no choice but to continue on to the end...}{}{92}{}{}
{607}{If you choose to do that, then I'll be forced to destroy you...}{}{5}{}{675}{}
{608}{No...I have a solution.  I can free you once and for all...}{}{5}{}{612}{}
{612}{[He looks at you, almost sadly.]  Truly, I wish there were freedom for me.  But I cannot let go of this life, knowing that I might be called back to its pain.  No, it seems I've no choice...}{[He looks at you, almost sadly.]  Truly, I wish there were freedom for me.  But I cannot let go of this life, knowing that I might be called back to its pain.  No, it seems I've no choice...}{}{93}{}{}
{613}{Then let us finish this once and for all...}{}{5}{}{-71}{}
{614}{The Vendigroth Device...it will sever you from this world forever...}{}{5}{in 5616}{618}{gf2674 1}
{615}{This weapon...it will sever you from this world forever...}{}{5}{in 2008}{618}{gf2675 1}
{618}{[Something like hope flares in his eyes. ]  Really?  You can sever the bonds which holds my soul to the lands of the living?  This object can actually do that?}{[Something like hope flares in his eyes. ]  Really?  You can sever the bonds which holds my soul to the lands of the living?  This object can actually do that?}{}{94}{}{}
{619}{Yes.  I can free you from the pain that you fear...}{}{5}{}{624}{}
{620}{I could.  But I'd rather kill you with my own hands...}{}{5}{}{-71}{}
{624}{[He bows his head, his shoulders sagging.]  So many years I've raged against the living.  All those years, and the distortion was in my own soul.  No man can see the nature of his flaws with diseased eyes...the contradiction lies within me.}{[He bows his head, his shoulders sagging.]  So many years I've raged against the living.  All those years, and the distortion was in my own soul.  No man can see the nature of his flaws with diseased eyes...the contradiction lies within me.}{}{95}{}{}
{625}{Let me end your journey, Kerghan.  Go to your rest.}{}{5}{}{630}{}
{630}{Yes.  I thank you...and I'm sorry.  So very, very sorry.  Perhaps some souls are born into death...they never knew how to live...}{Yes.  I thank you...and I'm sorry.  So very, very sorry.  Perhaps some souls are born into death...they never knew how to live...}{}{96}{}{}
